<title>USA: US rep wants plan against heating oil shortages.</title>
<headline>US rep wants plan against heating oil shortages.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rep. Joseph Kennedy, D-Massachusetts, said Monday he wanted the Energy Department to develop a contingency plan to deal with a potential heating oil supply shortage or price shock.</p>
<p>&quot;I think there's got to be some proactive steps that the secretary, I hope, will begin to outline, indicating that she's on top of it and is protecting the interests of the American consumer,&quot; Kennedy told reporters before a meeting with Energy Secretary Hazel O'Leary.</p>
<p>Kennedy and Democratic Sens. Joseph Lieberman and Christopher Dodd of Connecticut were meeting with O'Leary for an update on her talks with the industry and futures market regulators on the winter fuel supply outlook.</p>
